    "interactive_guide_EM9mhU": {
      "type": "interactive-guide",
      "blocks": {
        "guide_step_mahRAi": {
          "type": "guide_step",
          "settings": {
            "anchor_id": "cut",
            "nav_label": "4 Cs of Diamonds Charts",
            "desktop_pos": "left",
            "mobile_swap": "image_first",
            "col_width": 50,
            "gap_d": 50,
            "gap_m": 20,
            "pad_top": 10,
            "pad_bottom": 10,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Aug_19_2026_07_45_50_PM.png",
            "img_radius": 0,
            "img_border_w": 0,
            "img_border_color": "#eeeeee",
            "text_align_d": "flex-start",
            "text_align_m": "flex-start",
            "title": "4 Cs of Diamonds Charts",
            "title_color": "#111111",
            "title_size_d": 32,
            "title_size_m": 24,
            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>The 4 Cs of diamonds — cut, color, clarity, and carat — are the universal standards used to understand diamond quality. Each C represents a unique characteristic that contributes to a diamond’s beauty and brilliance.</p><p>• <strong>Cut:</strong> Graded from Ideal to Poor on the IGI scale.<br/>• <strong>Color:</strong> Graded from D (colorless) to Z (light yellow or brown).<br/>• <strong>Clarity:</strong> Graded from Flawless (FL) to Included (I3).<br/>• <strong>Carat:</strong> Measured in metric carats, where one carat equals 200 milligrams.</p>",
            "text_color": "#444444",
            "text_size_d": 15,
            "text_size_m": 13,
            "text_weight": "400",
            "text_lh": "1.6",
            "text_mb": 10,
            "show_callout": false,
            "callout_text": "Good quality cut which reflects some light while maintaining weight.",
            "callout_bg": "#1b3b36",
            "callout_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "callout_border_color": "#1b3b36",
            "callout_border_w": 0,
            "callout_radius": 2,
            "callout_size_d": 13,
            "callout_size_m": 12,
            "callout_weight": "400",
            "callout_pad_v": 16,
            "callout_pad_h": 20,
            "callout_mt": 16,
            "btn_label": "",
            "btn_link": "",
            "btn_bg": "#ffffff",
            "btn_text_color": "#111111",
            "btn_border_color": "#111111",
            "btn_bg_hover": "#111111",
            "btn_text_hover": "#ffffff",
            "btn_border_hover": "#111111",
            "btn_border_w": 1,
            "btn_radius": 0,
            "btn_size_d": 13,
            "btn_size_m": 12,
            "btn_weight": "500",
            "btn_pad_v": 12,
            "btn_pad_h": 24,
            "btn_mt": 14
          }
        },
        "guide_step_yTqhXq": {
          "type": "guide_step",
          "settings": {
            "anchor_id": "color",
            "nav_label": "Diamond Cut",
            "desktop_pos": "right",
            "mobile_swap": "image_first",
            "col_width": 50,
            "gap_d": 50,
            "gap_m": 20,
            "pad_top": 10,
            "pad_bottom": 10,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Aug_19_2026_07_54_00_PM.png",
            "img_radius": 0,
            "img_border_w": 0,
            "img_border_color": "#eeeeee",
            "text_align_d": "flex-start",
            "text_align_m": "flex-start",
            "title": "Diamond Cut",
            "title_color": "#111111",
            "title_size_d": 32,
            "title_size_m": 24,
            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>Cut is one of the most important factors that influences a diamond’s brilliance and sparkle. It refers to how precisely a diamond’s facets are shaped and arranged to interact with light. A well-crafted cut allows light to enter, reflect, and return through the top of the diamond, creating exceptional brightness, fire, and scintillation.</p><p>Unlike colour, clarity, and carat, which are determined during a diamond’s formation, cut quality depends on the expertise and precision of the diamond cutter. A superior cut enhances the diamond’s natural beauty, while a poorly cut diamond may lose light and appear less vibrant.</p>",
            "text_color": "#444444",
            "text_size_d": 15,
            "text_size_m": 13,
            "text_weight": "400",
            "text_lh": "1.6",
            "text_mb": 10,
            "show_callout": false,
            "callout_text": "Good quality cut which reflects some light while maintaining weight.",
            "callout_bg": "#1b3b36",
            "callout_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "callout_border_color": "#1b3b36",
            "callout_border_w": 0,
            "callout_radius": 2,
            "callout_size_d": 13,
            "callout_size_m": 12,
            "callout_weight": "400",
            "callout_pad_v": 16,
            "callout_pad_h": 20,
            "callout_mt": 16,
            "btn_label": "",
            "btn_link": "",
            "btn_bg": "#ffffff",
            "btn_text_color": "#111111",
            "btn_border_color": "#111111",
            "btn_bg_hover": "#111111",
            "btn_text_hover": "#ffffff",
            "btn_border_hover": "#111111",
            "btn_border_w": 1,
            "btn_radius": 0,
            "btn_size_d": 13,
            "btn_size_m": 12,
            "btn_weight": "500",
            "btn_pad_v": 12,
            "btn_pad_h": 24,
            "btn_mt": 14
          }
        },
        "guide_step_TH8Cjw": {
          "type": "guide_step",
          "settings": {
            "anchor_id": "clarity",
            "nav_label": "Diamond Color",
            "desktop_pos": "left",
            "mobile_swap": "image_first",
            "col_width": 50,
            "gap_d": 50,
            "gap_m": 20,
            "pad_top": 10,
            "pad_bottom": 10,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Aug_19_2026_08_00_54_PM.png",
            "img_radius": 0,
            "img_border_w": 0,
            "img_border_color": "#eeeeee",
            "text_align_d": "flex-start",
            "text_align_m": "flex-start",
            "title": "Diamond Color",
            "title_color": "#111111",
            "title_size_d": 32,
            "title_size_m": 24,
            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>Diamond color refers to the absence of color in a diamond. The less color a diamond has, the rarer and more valuable it becomes. IGI grades diamond color on a scale from <strong>D (Colorless) to Z (Light Yellow or Brown)</strong>, with each grade representing a subtle difference in color appearance.</p><p>The IGI Color Grading Scale includes:</p><ul><li><strong>D – F: Colorless</strong><br/>Diamonds in this range have exceptional transparency and appear completely colorless.</li><li><strong>G – J: Near Colorless</strong><br/>These diamonds show minimal color that is difficult to notice, offering excellent value and beauty.</li><li><strong>K – M: Faint Color</strong><br/>A slight warm tone becomes more visible while maintaining attractive brilliance.</li><li><strong>N – R: Very Light Color</strong><br/>Noticeable color tones begin to appear within the diamond.</li><li><strong>S – Z: Light Color</strong><br/>Diamonds display visible yellow or brown hues.</li></ul><p>Diamond color selection depends on personal preference, diamond size, shape, and the jewellery setting. Larger diamonds and certain shapes may reveal color more easily, making the right grade an important part of choosing the perfect diamond.</p>",
            "text_color": "#444444",
            "text_size_d": 15,
            "text_size_m": 13,
            "text_weight": "400",
            "text_lh": "1.6",
            "text_mb": 10,
            "show_callout": false,
            "callout_text": "Good quality cut which reflects some light while maintaining weight.",
            "callout_bg": "#1b3b36",
            "callout_text_color": "#ffffff",
            "callout_border_color": "#1b3b36",
            "callout_border_w": 0,
            "callout_radius": 2,
            "callout_size_d": 13,
            "callout_size_m": 12,
            "callout_weight": "400",
            "callout_pad_v": 16,
            "callout_pad_h": 20,
            "callout_mt": 16,
            "btn_label": "",
            "btn_link": "",
            "btn_bg": "#ffffff",
            "btn_text_color": "#111111",
            "btn_border_color": "#111111",
            "btn_bg_hover": "#111111",
            "btn_text_hover": "#ffffff",
            "btn_border_hover": "#111111",
            "btn_border_w": 1,
            "btn_radius": 0,
            "btn_size_d": 13,
            "btn_size_m": 12,
            "btn_weight": "500",
            "btn_pad_v": 12,
            "btn_pad_h": 24,
            "btn_mt": 14
          }
        },
        "guide_step_rFeQ8k": {
          "type": "guide_step",
          "settings": {
            "anchor_id": "clarity",
            "nav_label": "Diamond Clarity",
            "desktop_pos": "right",
            "mobile_swap": "image_first",
            "col_width": 50,
            "gap_d": 50,
            "gap_m": 20,
            "pad_top": 10,
            "pad_bottom": 10,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/ChatGPT_Image_Aug_19_2026_08_06_35_PM.png",
            "img_radius": 0,
            "img_border_w": 0,
            "img_border_color": "#eeeeee",
            "text_align_d": "flex-start",
            "text_align_m": "flex-start",
            "title": "Diamond Clarity",
            "title_color": "#111111",
            "title_size_d": 32,
            "title_size_m": 24,
            "title_weight": "500",
            "title_mb": 14,
            "body_text": "<p>Clarity refers to how free a diamond is from internal characteristics (<strong>inclusions</strong>) and external imperfections (<strong>blemishes</strong>). A diamond with higher clarity has fewer visible characteristics, allowing its natural beauty and brilliance to shine.</p><p>The IGI clarity scale ranges from <strong>Flawless (FL) to Included (I3)</strong>, with each grade representing the level of internal and surface features within the diamond. Most diamonds contain tiny characteristics that are not visible to the naked eye and do not affect their overall beauty.</p><p>The impact of inclusions depends on their <strong>size, number, and location</strong>. Features positioned beneath the top surface of the diamond may affect appearance more than those located near the edges. Each diamond has a unique clarity profile, making individual evaluation an important part of selecting the perfect stone.</p>",
            "text_color": "#444444",
            "text_size_d": 15,
            "text_size_m": 13,
            "text_weight": "400",
            "text_lh": "1.6",
            "text_mb": 10,
